Z||000010||BellaFiero||09-15-2000||10:12 AM||||Dead Man’s Curve, named so for the wicked incline and almost 90 degree turn that hugged the side of the mountain, had been used for years as a local gathering spot for teenagers. The Mustang Marauders and the Rice Revolution, as many of the body shop guys referred to them, had been using the bluff at the top of the curve to meet. With music blaring and alchohol flowing, it had become a weekend hangout. While subject to police hassle, the same youths showed up every weekend.<BR>It was Saturday, and the music thudded through the bluff like a dull monotone scream, like a freight train on rusted tracks. Techno and industrial clashed with rap and hip hop, and dirty looks were exchanged and the music melted into one another. Leather jackets and cuffed jeans stood far away from baggy Caffeine kick pants and bright neon shirts, bandanas and greasy hair stood out against the brightly colored backwards hats. The Mustangs, Camaros, and Firebirds sat with muscled pride, their hoods open and their engines like the constant growl of beasts.<BR>	Across the field, the Civics and Del Sols and Integras sat lowered in the grass like cheetahs. Windows banners and oriental script covered their pearl white and cherry red paint jobs, and the thick bright chrome of bumble bee exhaust poked from under the rear bumpers. <BR>Earlier that night, an Autozone had been driven into, glass and frame bent around the body of a small compact car. The store had been looted, packages torn apart and parts missing from the overturned shelves in the back room. Wall and plaster littered the tiled floor, and glass shards were everywhere. It was a heated debate who would’ve ripped off the auto store, and where the parts would be sold for cheap on the street.<BR> The wind was strong this night, blowing over the bluff, leaves stirring and dust clouds forming at the feet of the teens. Fog lights and driving lights, hi-beams, and the bright yellow of parking lights all lit up the field with a stadium’s brightness.  Lovers embraced while gearheads talked shop, and the music thumped in hard echos.<BR>At the bottom of the cliff, revving on and off, letting the engine scream and fall off, then scream back up, it’s tachometer like a knife that cut it’s way ever downward, a slash of red sat in the darkness. The perfect, deep paint job was marred with a <BR> Silver Corvette’s paint etched along the door and fenders. A Honda emblem sat imbedded in the front fascia, limb of fallen prey stuck between the sharpness of a predator’s fangs. The engine revved up and held it’s RPMs, loud and harsh in the night as her oil bubbled beneath the deck lid. The temperature needle rose high, to detonation, and held, as the car’s fluids pressed through ancient, frayed hoses.  Antifreeze dumped itself by the gallon on the engine, thick clouds of steam issuing forth from the heat. <BR>Up ahead, the bright neon lights of the Ricers and Marauders, the blaring music and the constant THUMP THUMP THUMP beckoned her. Tires crept across the gravel on the side of the road, hungry tread eager to melt in blissful heat against the street. The spoiler almost stretched as it lowered itself, screws loosening and angling the thick spread of fiberglass. They tightened, rusty, and as they turned the rust fell away from brilliant silver beneath. The tear on the rear fascia pressed together, puckering and dissapearing as the engine held it’s rev. The lights flared brightly, and the overhead dome light clicked on. The shifter moved slowly, as the clutch depressed itself.<BR>	…Thick chunks of glass were pressed out of the right rear tire as it began to spin…<BR>	… hoses melted back together, rubber reforming under the immense heat of the engine compartment, rubber fragments gripping to one another…<BR>	… the screech of the accelerating car was not of tires on pavement, although the smoke issuing from the back was. The sound of hatred and rage, of broken fate, was of a girl’s…<BR>	… the bloody scrawl across the top of the windshield was caught by the overhead street lamps... 'Cauldron Born' …<BR>||||reg||1
